<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Drobeta-Turnu Severin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Turnu Severin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Drobeta-Turnu Severin is a city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, just below the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-gates">Iron Gates</a> gorge. On the site of the Roman town of Drobeta, where Apollodorus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trajan">Trajan</a>'s bridge across the Danube in 105, a medieval fortress, Severin, was raised, and it was the seat of the Hungarian Banate of Severin from the 13th century. The town later became part of Wallachia and grew as a Danube port in the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/drobeta-turnu-severin.jpg" alt="Drobeta-Turnu Severin" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boxenhorst · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cultural-Palace-Teodor-Costescu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
